From fadfeb884d2a1c95951ebb04b40fb9d87f58bdf3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Craterbrain <58347640+Craterbrain@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 15:20:31 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] PlaitOS: Material Symbols for every PlaitOS row; style late
 and missing icons

- Every PlaitOS row (the PlaitOS pages and the PlaitOS rows on Lock screen,
  Power menu, Gestures, Display, Sound, Notifications and 3-button
  navigation) gets a Material Symbols Rounded icon that fits it, generated by
  plait-os/scripts/settings-icons.py (ic_plait_sym_*, tinted like Settings'
  own icons). The crDroid drawables (ic_plait_*), several of which did not
  fit their rows, are removed.
- Icons a controller sets after the page was styled (Internet's Wi-Fi level,
  SIMs, Data Saver, and rows on pages built from code) are styled when the
  row is bound: only the view gets a styled copy of a symbol drawable; app
  icons and anything else keep their artwork, and the row's color stays
  stable while scrolling, even with random colors on.
- With a style on, stock rows that had no icon on pages where every other
  row has one get one (connectivity checks, mobile network security,
  Certificate Transparency downloads, attestation and Widevine provisioning,
  connection preferences, UWB, additional system updates, developer options,
  Linux terminal, accessibility shortcuts, text-to-speech, assistant long
  press). Style 0 stays exactly stock.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
